<Project>
  <!--
    Rule Engine release versioning — ONE source for every runtime artifact.

    RuleEngineVersion is the release. It drives AssemblyVersion, FileVersion and
    InformationalVersion of EDP.RuleRuntime (core) and EDP.RuleRuntime.Crm (plug-in), so the two
    assemblies can never disagree about which release they are.

    Bump it on EVERY change that ships to Dataverse: the sandbox caches plug-in assemblies by
    version, so re-uploading different code under an existing version can keep serving the old
    code. The org already holds an older build labelled 1.0.24, which is why 1.1.0 skips past it.

    DataversePluginPackageVersion is NOT the release version. It is the version of the plug-in
    package RECORD in Dataverse (qdb_EdpRuleRuntime), fixed when the record was created on
    2026-08-19 and immutable thereafter ("You can't change the name and version of the plug-in
    package (on the server) once created" — Microsoft Learn, Build and package plug-in code).
    The nuspec carries the record's version so an update never looks like an attempt to change
    it; "the version of the plug-in package or plug-in assembly is not a factor in any upgrade
    behaviors" (Microsoft Learn, Create and register a plug-in package). The release is
    identified by the assembly version inside the package. See deploy/A7-RELEASE-PROCEDURE.md.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <RuleEngineVersion>1.1.0</RuleEngineVersion>
    <DataversePluginPackageVersion>1.0.0</DataversePluginPackageVersion>

    <Version>$(RuleEngineVersion)</Version>
    <AssemblyVersion>$(RuleEngineVersion).0</AssemblyVersion>
    <FileVersion>$(RuleEngineVersion).0</FileVersion>
    <InformationalVersion>$(RuleEngineVersion)</InformationalVersion>
  </PropertyGroup>
</Project>
